  "text": "Here is the step-by-step calculation to determine the savings and remaining amount.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate total expenses for rent, food, and transport.**\n$$ \\text{Total Expenses} = \\text{Rent} + \\text{Food} + \\text{Transport} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Expenses} = 1248 + 468 + 109 $$\n$$ \\text{Total Expenses} = 1825 $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the amount remaining after these three expenses.**\n$$ \\text{Remaining Amount} = \\text{Income} - \\text{Total Expenses} $$\n$$ \\text{Remaining Amount} = 3348 - 1825 $$\n$$ \\text{Remaining Amount} = 1523 $$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the monthly savings.**\nThe person saves 20% of what remains after the three expenses (which is 1523).\n$$ \\text{Savings} = 20\\% \\times 1523 $$\n$$ \\text{Savings} = 0.20 \\times 1523 $$\n$$ \\text{Savings} = 304.6 $$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate how much is left after saving.**\nThis is the amount remaining from Step 2 minus the savings calculated in Step 3.\n$$ \\text{Left After Saving} = \\text{Remaining Amount} - \\text{Savings} $$\n$$ \\text{Left After Saving} = 1523 - 304.6 $$\n$$ \\text{Left After Saving} = 1218.4 $$\n\nAnswer: 304.6, 1218.4",
